  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Puck tag – protect your puck",
  "description": "A box of about 10 × 10 metres and four players. Three have a puck each and protect it, the fourth is the chaser without a puck. The chaser tries to win a puck within the rules. Whoever loses their puck becomes the new chaser and tries to win a puck from someone else.\n\nKeep it going for about five minutes. With more players: make more boxes, or have two chasers in a bigger box. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Put your body between the chaser and the puck."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Look up – where can you skate with the puck away from the chaser?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Chaser: win the puck with the stick, not the body."
    }
  ],
